Saved gateway connection-test settings
======================================

Testing a saved gateway forwards its saved vendor options to the same adapter
construction path used by live operations. This includes explicit use_ssl
selection on custom ports. The explicit test certificate-verification override
still takes precedence over the saved verify_ssl field; neither is rewritten.

A shared settings projection protects adapter identity, destination, credential
and certificate-verification fields against settings collisions. Matching is
case-insensitive. Existing forbidden write-control options remain excluded.
Valid vendor options remain available. Historical stored JSON is not rewritten.
Absent or empty settings retain existing defaults. Cross-organization requests
remain refused before adapter creation.

Before/after qualification uses actual encrypted PostgreSQL rows and local
HTTP/TLS peers with real MikroTik and pfSense clients. Only the fixture hostname
is relocated to loopback; clients select the real scheme and custom port.
The old path can send HTTP authentication despite a saved MikroTik HTTPS choice.
The repaired path honors all eight saved-protocol/peer combinations. Verification
is deliberately disabled in these transport-selection cases; they do not prove
certificate trust. Four-vendor settings/identity checks additionally use adapter
factory doubles, with actual database rows and explicit trust overrides.

Constructor exception mapping is covered by GATEWAY-CONSTRUCTION-FAILURES.
Saved-test resource authority and stale results are covered by
GATEWAY-TEST-AUTHORITY. Current caller/session/grant revalidation, broader
provider metadata and other diagnostic logs remain separate.
No hardware operations, schema changes or dependency upgrades are performed.
See GATEWAY-HTTPS-POLICY, GATEWAY-TEST-LIFECYCLE and GATEWAY-TEST-DIAGNOSTICS.
